TunaHome is written from scratch. It is not based on another launcher.

Its themes, branding and self-updater follow TunaReceive
(https://github.com/bigtunafish9943/TunaReceive, GPL-3.0), from the same
author: the theme names and colours, the fish mark, and the update checks
were carried over from that project.

Libraries: AndroidX RecyclerView (Apache License 2.0) and the Kotlin
standard library (Apache License 2.0).

Icons: the settings, TV and download symbols are from Google's Material
Symbols (Apache License 2.0).

Fonts: the fonts in app/src/main/assets/fonts are from Google Fonts
(https://github.com/google/fonts), under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Each font's licence is beside it in app/src/main/assets/fonts/licences.
They were trimmed to Latin characters to keep the app small; the
names and licences are unchanged.

Wallpaper apps: projectivyapi/ is Projectivy Launcher's wallpaper
plugin interface, copied unchanged from
https://github.com/spocky/projectivy-plugin-wallpaper-provider
(Apache License 2.0, see projectivyapi/LICENSE). It lets wallpaper
apps such as Aerial Views show their videos behind TunaHome.

Video: AndroidX Media3 (Apache License 2.0).
